Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S05
Scenario title: Specification Document Review
Initial workflow description:
An engineer reviews a specification document to check whether new features are reflected correctly and whether there are typos or missing details.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What event or condition triggers the start of a specification document review — for example, a new document version being published, a change request being approved, or a scheduled review date?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "How does the engineer determine which parts of the document to review — do they use a checklist, compare against a previous version using a diff, or read the entire document from scratch?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "When an issue is found, how is it categorized or prioritized — is there a defined classification scheme such as severity levels or issue types, and does the category affect how the issue is handled next?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "Where and how are review findings recorded and communicated to the relevant parties — for example, inline document comments, a separate issue tracker, a structured review form, or email?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "Besides the reviewing engineer, who else participates in the review process, and who is responsible for resolving the issues that are identified?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "What criteria must be met for a review to be considered complete — is a formal sign-off required, and is a follow-up review conducted after corrections are made?"
  }
]
